WEBVTT

00:04:26.038 --> 00:04:30.121
I walked with my cane
and my ankle brace and a backpack

00:04:30.163 --> 00:04:32.079
on trips in six continents.

00:04:32.579 --> 00:04:36.163
I pitched overhand
in a weekly softball game

00:04:36.163 --> 00:04:38.204
that I started in Central Park,

00:04:38.246 --> 00:04:39.496
and home in New York,

00:04:39.496 --> 00:04:41.538
I became a journalist and an author,

00:04:41.538 --> 00:04:44.663
typing hundreds of thousands
of words with one finger.

00:04:45.413 --> 00:04:46.663
A friend pointed out to me

00:04:46.704 --> 00:04:49.246
that all of my big stories
mirrored my own,

00:04:49.246 --> 00:04:53.079
each centering on a life
that had changed in an instant,

00:04:53.079 --> 00:04:55.788
owing, if not to a crash,
then to an inheritance,

00:04:55.829 --> 00:04:58.579
a swing of the bat,
a click of the shutter, an arrest.

00:04:58.621 --> 00:05:01.871
Each of us had a before and an after.